{"author_association": "NONE", "body": "> Acknowledged. We took community analysis at face value, including outputs from prior LLM-assisted solvers, without sufficiently questioning whether the data was independently verifiable. That's a fair criticism.\n> \n> What we can verify ourselves, without relying on anything posted here: the Phase 2 and 3 decryptions, the 7 SalPhaseIon tokens, K_C1, K_I1, the full L4 decoding derived independently via crib-drag, including the part that ends with \"CIAO BELLA O.\" None of that came from this repo.\n> \n> The warning is noted. We know what we own.\n\n@EnigmAnderson \u2014 independent researcher here. I reproduced your \n\"905 bytes beneath the garbled section\" reference cleanly:\n\nchain4_decrypted (1151B, SHA e4269ed5...) splits at byte 246:\n- head[0:246] entropy 7.150 (structured)\n- tail[246:1151] entropy 7.790 (high)\n- SHA256(tail) = 9f06936a48d393c858a6fdce281540946e8f5365d632ad756c280b400c9d632c\n\nI've exhaustively tested K_I1 candidates derived from {8 priv-class \nscalars \u00d7 header[0:246] bytes \u00d7 Phase 3.2.2 literal phrases \u00d7 K_H \non-chain artifacts} \u2014 ~62 transforms, zero anchor matches.\n\nYou wrote \"we know K_I1, and K_I1 alone was never meant to open the \nlast door\" \u2014 this suggests K_I1 is recoverable but is one of multiple \nrequired operands.\n\nWithout asking for the K_I1 value: is K_I1 derivable from public \nartifacts only, or does it depend on something external (off-chain \nhint, deleted gist, another decoded layer not in the README)?\n\nA single-bit structural answer (yes/no on \"publicly derivable\") would \nbe enormously useful and exposes nothing.", "created_at": "2026-04-26T12:01:14Z", "html_url": "https://github.com/puzzlehunt/gsmgio-5btc-puzzle/issues/87#issuecomment-4321973431", "id": 4321973431, "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/puzzlehunt/gsmgio-5btc-puzzle/issues/87", "minimized": null, "node_id": "IC_kwDOD23F088AAAABAZwUtw", "performed_via_github_app": null, "pin": null, "reactions": {"+1": 0, "-1": 0, "confused": 0, "eyes": 0, "heart": 0, "hooray": 0, "laugh": 0, "rocket": 0, "total_count": 0, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/puzzlehunt/gsmgio-5btc-puzzle/issues/comments/4321973431/reactions"}, "updated_at": "2026-04-26T12:01:14Z", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/puzzlehunt/gsmgio-5btc-puzzle/issues/comments/4321973431", "user": {"avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29788148?v=4", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/events{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/andersonbig", "id": 29788148, "login": "andersonbig", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI5Nzg4MTQ4", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/andersonbig", "user_view_type": "public"}}
